# UI System Rules

## UI Design Agent

For implementation and living “how it works now” state, attach
`.cursor/rules/uiDesignAgent.mdc` and read `docs/styles/CURRENT-STATE.md` first. This file
holds **hard boundaries**; CURRENT-STATE holds the **current mechanism snapshot** and delta log.
When public exports, import graph, or style hierarchy change, update this file and CURRENT-STATE
together.

## Separation

```text
design-tokens (no React)
      |
  +---+---+
  |       |
ui-web  ui-native
```

- Do **not** build one universal UI package for web and native.
- Web and native component implementations stay platform-specific.
- Shared design language comes only from `design-tokens`.

## design-tokens

- Framework-agnostic. Forbidden dependencies: React, react-native, api, state, auth.
- Emits TS token objects (for RN/JS) and CSS custom properties (for web/Next.js).

## ui-web / ui-native

- Allowed: design-tokens, platform runtime, headless/RN primitives, utils, constants, types.
  `@azes/ui-web` may depend on `@mui/material` and Emotion (ADR-009). It must not depend on
  `@mui/material-nextjs` (that package peers on Next.js).
- Forbidden: api, Redux/state, auth, business domains. `design-tokens` must not depend on MUI.
- Apps consume `@azes/ui-web` / `@azes/ui-native` only — never Radix/MUI/Ant/NativeBase
  components directly. Exceptions are listed in ADR-009 (`InitColorSchemeScript` and
  `@mui/material-nextjs` in `realestate`; deep icon imports in `azes-ui`).

## ui-web subpaths (ADR-010)

- Public entries: `@azes/ui-web` (core) plus `/settings`, `/navigation`, `/layout`, `/icons`,
  `/data-grid`, `/charts`, `/forms`, `/feedback`, `/locale`.
- Core (`src/theme`, `src/components`, `src/catalog.ts`) never imports a subpath folder.
- `layout` may import `navigation` and `settings`. `icons`, `forms`, `data-grid`, `charts`,
  `feedback`, `locale` import core only (settings may compose feedback for `AzesUiProvider`).
- ui-web never imports a router, `@azes/permissions`, i18n, api, state or auth. Router and
  access are injected (`AzesRouterAdapter`, `AzesAccessContext`).
- MUI only: no Tailwind, Radix, styled-components, vanilla-extract, framer-motion, ApexCharts,
  Iconify or other styling/design-system libraries (`docs/styles/19-dependencies.md`).

## Style decision hierarchy

```text
Global decision -> tokens/theme -> theme.components overrides -> AZES component -> sx (local only)
```

Permanent design rules never live in `sx`. Colors from `theme.vars`; sizes from tokens; layout
code uses `--azes-layout-*` variables, never px literals.

## Agent rules

- Prefer wrapping primitives inside the AZES design system over exposing third-party APIs.
- Keep underlying primitive libraries replaceable without forcing app changes.
- Do not add business/API logic to UI packages.
- `docs/styles/legacy/` is frozen. Update the numbered files in `docs/styles/` instead.

See `docs/styles/README.md`, `docs/architecture/ui-architecture.md` and ADRs 004 / 008–016.
